editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-11-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-12-> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
