editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-20-> - **Paper custody:** Karis has the flat under one arm and the hide under the other; inside the flat are six counted/re-taped rows with the original technician's sheet restored to the end of row two, plus the completion report and her copy; Vastin's copied page remains in its oilcloth inside her coat; Cael laid his hand on it once, on the rise, and gave it back (coordinator ruling: the author's beat is kept) (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:141–149,155–157`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:207,271–291`). Karis also has the dead surveyor's ledger/notebook; Seln's case remains shut on his own strap (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:183–187`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-21-> - **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-22-> - **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-23-> - **Oryn:** she and the brown mule are north of the fork on the reverse circuit; she has her linen and crossbow with one bolt. Her stated route is five gates, the ford and Millrace, where she expects the six in three weeks; she still owes Cael the proper reading and expects “all of it” from the archive (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:63–81,171–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-24-> - **Money/objects:** purse 138; reserve sealed; sixty yards of four-strand still owed; Pike's thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt; no cordage was bought (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`). Oryn's empty bowl is Brom's to carry (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:221–223`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-25-> - **Progression:** ten fragments, deployment THIRTY-TWO (coordinator ruling: one Ember grain at the mark and one Wind burst away, both at the cut); Shadow sealed, Anchor still two, Tide unused, no self-read, no eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:133–163,223–227`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:205–211`). Vastin has shown Iron Wall once; Cael witnessed it but did not acquire it (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-26-> - **Treswick/day:** it is a little before noon on day 281, at the top of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. The six have seen a bluff, river loops, three tiered walls and the pale steady station light; Cael turned his eyes to the lowest wall, and Lira has not yet performed the packet's unasked matching discipline (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–269`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,43`).
