editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-18-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-19-### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-20-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-21-- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the hundred and thirty-first morning, after the Book 7 hearth scene at the lower inn. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; Oryn's letter arrived through a hand's depth of snow on day 131. Book 8 continues later that morning. The Book 8 count remains day 131 to day 308. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-23-- **The five at Lowmarch:** Lira (Wind, Iron R1 formal) has all eight left-forearm marks whole, but the arm is slung high and holds nothing until Oryn says; the right ankle is taped and unmended. She carries Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt and cannot span it herself. Brom (Iron Skin, Copper formal) has the right shoulder mended twice, not a third, held in four yards of webbing by the drover's turn; the older healer says it will do. Karis (Ember, **Iron Rank Three**) has 52 copied sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall), the dead surveyor's ledger, the carter's map with four circles and the line off the hide, and the Ternhall straightedge; her voice is whole and her larger hypothesis remains unspoken and unentered. Seln (Shadow, Bronze; fifteen years' service) has his **locked case**, carried shut for twelve years and unopened. Cael has Hesk's brass straightedge and satchel. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-24-- **Objects/accounts:** the tarred-canvas kit case, strap, cord knotted at the fives, unused stake 32 with stroke/bar and bright turned point, and mallet are at the back-room table; the dead man's ledger is shut beside them. Three boxes stand at the warm wall. The cart-and-gelding reserve remains sealed under five thumbprints in the third box, separate from the 96-mark living purse. The Fallow hundred and Stair 300 remain in Pike's box, unmarked and not crew-payable debts. The ferryman is owed 60 yards of four-strand rope, not wanted before the thaw. The forty-mark axe-head fence is taken and not begun. Teague forfeited the four-mark weir slip. The six-mark back room is paid through the cold term; hearth space is covered by standing-money. Two westbound letters cost one copper apiece. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-25-- **Letters/animals:** Hesk's brass and note and Oryn's bark have arrived. Letters to Hesk and Vell went west on the last ferry; Ephram's is deferred to the first boat of the thaw. The brown mule is with the five. Oryn has the grey jenny and the thirty-foot three-strand rope. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:26:- **Oryn:** last located at Thornwater, with route work north next. The old debt ran Cael→Oryn and is **PAID**: three self-readings and the full telling. Her withheld answer was never a debt. Her exact letter is: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` Lira's arm waits on Oryn's in-person word. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:27:- **Teague's crew:** stays through the cold term at Lowmarch's upper inn: four practitioners plus the older healer of no Path, all unnamed except Teague. His exact term is: `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` He has the cold road; the five have the axe-head fence. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-28-- **The Quieting:** four sites lie on one straight edge of the map. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was seen and paced from outside at **440 yards and two strides** radius, behind registry-iron stake 34 repeated one per pace. It is unentered, unnamed, undated and untested; its grey central upright is unresolved and its effect unknown. `Someone made this pattern.` was said once and not answered. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-29-- **Pike/the Compact:** Pike has nine completed lines under the five names; the ninth is the Stair and reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The first-snow season line is written with no number against it. The five names remain **eleventh**. The Compact has a Fallow completion report, the Stair rim's observations and a clerk's packet saying the crew kept the kit; it does not know that fragments work inside. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4] It has reached across the Line twice: on paper (the Fallow completion report) and in person (the six on the Stair's rim). The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-30-- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-31-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-32-### Ending (source Ch24, dawn of the 308th; must hand off to Book 9)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-33-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-34-- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-35-- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-51-Dates are the Line's count. A source chapter is shown as (S*n*).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-52-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-53-1. **KEEP — The cold-term frame (S1, 131st–264th).** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The cold stay is priced [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-54-2. **KEEP — Pike's cold-term board and the fence (140th).** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-55-3. **KEEP — The river is a road (161st); the kit on the table.** The cord is knotted at the fives, the stake is number thirty-two, plus the mallet and the field ledger with the radius line. The Stair's designation sits in an unreadable index above the stopped line "third site confirmed on bearing". Karis learns the kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-56-4. **KEEP — The anomaly (168th).** The yard paces forty-two strides for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for Cael, three times. The Ternhall edge reads a hair short in his hand and Hesk's edge a hair long. Karis's ruler sentence is said twice: a rule, then not a rule. Logged: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-57-5. **KEEP — The thaw (230th–264th).** The ice goes. The Thornwater road opens. Karis says her sentence about west "in pieces since the fence", and in full on the 263rd.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-58-6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her first stops after the thaw [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:59:7. **KEEP — Six at Lowmarch (268th).** 118 marks (the mule's shed and the rope-house roof). Karis makes her case to six: the carvings are instructions; the index; west; **Treswick and the Deepstacks named**; the scholars' provision; "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **KEEP — the closing log (270th)**, verbatim (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-60-8. **KEEP — The ferry (277th).** Vastin arrives alone, in a brown coat, with an ash stick, a pack mended with cord and a bad knee. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." Pike prices him: "What'd he do?" → "Then he's nothing yet." He pays a copper and a half for bread. Teague reads his hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-61-9. **KEEP — The long table (277th midday).** The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, their first words ever. The short thing: resigned or walked. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence; Vastin's new fact is "Cannot. There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail dead-ends at Treswick. Vastin has nothing to do afterwards. "Why us." Oryn on the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that can cross the Line. Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only: "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks; Vastin's close (§10). The ferry goes west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-62-10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-63-11. **KEEP — The slip (278th).** Clearance at the cut below the shoulder hold, twenty. "Ours" twice. Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin is not on the sheet and walks at the back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-64-12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-65-13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (the date matches his Kindling day; "six years" is the office's survey-record rounding; no numeric span since Kindling is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-66-14. **KEEP — The fork-stone (280th evening–281st first light).** Oryn's terms: "I'm not an archive person"; the city she left; "Leaving and routing are different verbs." "Three weeks" (Seln). **The promise** is written in the log and read back. She prices everyone. The Millrace rendezvous. "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with her. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. Treswick comes into view from the rise; the light on the crown is not looked at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-67-15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-68-16. **KEEP — Treswick's outer district (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts and does not ask. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of the crew looks in their own way. "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." "They shoe by the tier." The road to the registry crosses the square, and the promise holds. Seln's report: the quarry; the provision; hands by count, up to four; the clerk; the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." The close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-69-17. **KEEP — Cleon at noon (283rd).** "Off floors." / "Fifty-two sheets." His terms. He stops a step late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-70-18. **KEEP — The provision (284th).** Four hands go up by count: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin. Seln is not on the count. The square is avoided by Seln's route. The clerk does not ask and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull** ("Four hands." / "Four." / "Right."). The iron door. Cleon pulls the iron to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-71-19. **KEEP — The Deepstacks (284th).** Cleon is already reading. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. "Older than [UNBOUND]." "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael is unfiled for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-72-20. **KEEP — The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25; Gate 27): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration enters that Seln did not lie. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:73:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-74-22. **KEEP — The alley (290th, dusk).** Six faceless attackers: four above with a crossbow, two below with staves, one of the four a signaller on the landing. Vastin roots the cut wall to wall ("there is no round"). Nobody declares. Brom with a rock, Lira's drop, Cael still at the plane's foot ("the reason"), Seln's weighted cord from the roof. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave; none taken, no faces. Costs: Karis's left hand (a step's edge), bound by Brom with thread and teeth because no healer inside the gate would touch it; Vastin spent, the knee again. **The Iron-Wall notice** (§10). "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." Not told. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-75-23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-76-24. **KEEP — Dividers (292nd).** Hesk's parcel and note. The meal: four marks, two cups kept for Karis and Oryn, Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"); 130 marks. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." The first inventory written inside walls (§12 C10). **The station's light is "not steady" for a count of one**: a pressure, "an instrument turning toward him". It becomes the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross; the promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-77-25. **KEEP — The leaf (293rd morning).** It is read aloud **once** by Karis (§9). The chronicle leaf is **marked**. Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers: two pages. The copy with the gap drawn. "Older. Made. Us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-78-26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-79-27. **KEEP — The list of parts (294th) and Cleon's goodbye at the bell:** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-80-28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-81-29. **KEEP — Force seen (298th morning).** The meadow cart: the frame lined up heel to palm, a body's length; the wrist clicks; the young one's cloth. "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
--
