editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-344-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:345:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-346-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:347:### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-348-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-349-1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-350-2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-351-3. **Karis's copy and finding (S15):** "and the" [gap drawn] "set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it." / *Older. Made. Us.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-352-4. **Vastin's page (S3):** "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-353-5. **The technician's sheet (S3):** "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —" [brush bar]. Karis's note: *not read*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-354-6. **The surveyor's remark (S5):** "Behaves as device. Cannot be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-355-7. **Directive and objection (S20):** "Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat." / "Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat." / Vastin: "Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-370-21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-371-22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-372-23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-373-24. **Vastin's papers (S8):** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-374-25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-375-26. **The rate (S19 log):** "Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-376-27. **The contract (S17):** "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." / Force: "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
