editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:378:### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-379-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-380-- Karis (B7 edition `chapter-52.md:311`): `A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-381-- Karis (B7 edition `chapter-57.md:99`; `chapter-60.md:251`): `Three points make a line. Four make an argument.` / `Someone made this pattern.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-382-- Oryn (B7 edition `chapter-58.md:51–55`; `chapter-60.md:215,229`): `Find me at Thornwater.` / `Bring the map.` Her letter: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` / `Six, by letter.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-383-- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:67`): `Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-384-- Teague and Pike (B7 edition `chapter-59.md:199,221–225`): `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` / `I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-385-- Vastin (B6): "I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-386-- The still-place inventory (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:39`): `One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.` Oryn's order (B7 edition `chapter-55.md:289`): `Write it down and stop touching it.` The Tide rule (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:37`): `ask first, every time`. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-387-- The kit's ledger (B7 edition `chapter-52.md:223`): `third site confirmed on bearing`. The audio rule remains `the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-388-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:### Tier C — source-fixed lines and closers (keep verbatim)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-390-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-391-- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. Since my Kindling I've stayed out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-392-- **Thornwater:** "Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off." / "Will you mend it." / "Lie still" / "It's an arm. Use it. It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year and then it won't. Don't fall on it." / "I don't know what that is." … "Neither do you. Write that down too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:393:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-394-- **S4 lesson and log:** "The wall held the line," … "And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." … "I have never once in forty years needed someone else to be the reason." / "You do now," / "I know fields. I don't know packs." … "I'll learn or I won't." Log: "Vastin fought. He rooted the road and nearly got eaten for it — a wall's no good if you're the only thing making noise behind it. He knows fields. He doesn't know packs. He'll learn or he won't. Watched an Iron Wall go up two feet from me. Filed it. Note the day: an Archmarshal took a wound out here and there was no one to report it to. He looked almost free. Almost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-395-- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-396-- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-397-- **S7 log:** "Ran the reading on myself again. Same nothing at the center. I think the reading can't do it — you can't measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement. I need an instrument for what doesn't move. Karis says there's a man in Treswick who reads how things are built. Maybe that's the instrument. Maybe I'm about to hand a stranger the one question I've never let anyone hold. Tomorrow. The walls are close enough now to have a color." ("color" stands in the log, per ruling 19.) Also: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." / "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-398-- **S8:** "Entered by count. That's the door." Close: "Last time we walked into a place like this," … "it took four years and a hearing to walk out." [OWNER-pending #53] / "Last time we didn't know what we were looking for." / "Do we now?" / "A name and a reason," … "Older than the walls, under our feet, and nobody's read it because nobody's had a reason to look and a person who could read it in the same lifetime." … "That's us. That's the whole reason it's still buried. We're the first ones who are both." (On "four years" see §12 C2: this is the one place where Cael's spoken rounding stands.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-399-- **S9:** "Off floors," / "Fifty-two sheets." / "Four hands," / "Four." / "Right." / the log: "Lira looked at the whole ladder from the top of it and it didn't pull. She priced it. She's carrying a box."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-400-- **S10:** "Older than [UNBOUND]," / "I know that hand." / "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong." / "Give me a week." / "I'm sorry," / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody." Log: "Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-401-- **S11 close:** "You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." … "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." … "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." … "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since." Also: "You think Karis is right? That it's all built on something?" / "I think we're about to find out." / "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." / Seln: "I looked at it." / log: "Brom was offered the life. He picked up the box." / "Seln looked at it. Decided nothing."
--
