editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-460-- **Cael lies still for no one but Oryn,** and she has read him three times (sack, table, marsh's edge) until Millrace. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling — in the edition's Book 7 Oryn's hands were on Cael for several surface reads that found nothing (the mountain; the ford at Oxhollow; the stake), for the long reading on the 100th (the table), and at the Hall on the 120th (the marsh's edge); Cael has read Oryn twice, each time after asking and an explicit yes.] **Oryn does not read Cael** before Millrace's deep reading; she reads his ribs' surface at most.
