    20	
    21	He waited the afternoon there, because the district where the unranked were allowed was where a hand waited for a researcher, and he had decided at a long table to be a hand and meant to be a good one. The stair's foot had a bench on it for people who waited, and he sat on it with two carters' boys sent up with messages, and was, for an afternoon, exactly what they were, and watched the second gate do the thing it did.
