     9	It was wider than he had judged from the rise, and it ran brown and quick with the thaw of a whole moor in it. A bridge went over, long and low, with five piers standing in the water. He counted them twice, since Karis would ask. The roadway was only wide enough for one cart, with a bay built out over each pier where a person on foot could stand aside; and beyond the last pier there were two square towers with an arch between them, and the grey wall going away on both hands along the bank.
