   191	He had known it, of course. An officer of his grade did not arrive; he was announced, by a form, four days before, and the form went to the very people whom he came to look at. So he had ridden for forty years through streets that had been swept the day before, past whitewashed kerbs, to offices where every book lay squared on its desk and a man stood at the sill with his cap in his hand. He had allowed for it, as a careful officer allows for the known error of a scale, and had supposed that he could subtract the whitewash and arrive at the street.
   192	
